      <math display="block" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"> <mtable class="align" columnalign="left right left" columnspacing="0 0" displaystyle="true" intent=":system-of-equations"> <mtr> <mtd intent=":equation-label"> <mtext> (1) </mtext> </mtd> <mtd intent=":pause-medium"/> <mtd> <msup> <mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi> <mi>𝑧</mi> </msup> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">=</mo> <msup> <mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi> <mi>𝑥</mi> </msup> <mspace width="0.167em"/> <mrow> <mo fence="true" lspace="0" rspace="0.167em" symmetric="true">(</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal"> cos </mi> <mspace width="0.167em"/> <mi>𝑦</mi> <mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">+</mo> <mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi> <mspace width="0.167em"/> <mi mathvariant="normal"> sin </mi> <mspace width="0.167em"/> <mi>𝑦</mi> <mo fence="true" lspace="0" rspace="0" symmetric="true">)</mo> </mrow> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd intent=":equation-label"> <mtext> (2) </mtext> </mtd> <mtd intent=":pause-medium"/> <mtd> <msup> <mi>𝑧</mi> <mi>𝛼</mi> </msup> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">=</mo> <msup> <mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi> <mrow> <mi>𝛼</mi> <mspace width="0.167em"/> <mi mathvariant="normal"> ln </mi> <mspace width="0.167em"/> <mi>𝑧</mi> </mrow> </msup> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd colspan="3"> <mtext> Equations (1) and (2) lead to the following interesting results: </mtext> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd intent=":equation-label"> <mtext> (3) </mtext> </mtd> <mtd intent=":pause-medium"/> <mtd> <msup> <mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi> <mrow> <mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi> <mi>𝜋</mi> </mrow> </msup> <mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">+</mo> <mn>1</mn> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">=</mo> <mn>0</mn> </mtd> </mtr> <mtr> <mtd intent=":equation-label"> <mtext> (∗) </mtext> </mtd> <mtd intent=":pause-medium"/> <mtd> <msup> <mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi> <mi mathvariant="normal">i</mi> </msup> <mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">=</mo> <msup> <mi mathvariant="normal">e</mi> <mrow> <mo lspace="0" r